WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.840
When do you go at Red and stop at Green?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.560
When you're eating of Watermelon.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.940
Ever wondered why traffic lights are coloured the way they are?

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.620
You may probably say that Red represents danger.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.020
Green is for safety, and who cares for Yellow!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.080
What could be the real reason?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.800
Let's find out!

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.140
Let's say we were to select the colours for traffic signals.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.660
What factors should we keep in mind?

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.040
Our main focus should be the high visibility of colours,

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.760
as this is extremely important for the drivers.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.920
It could be for a clear view from a distance

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.780
or for visibility during extreme weather conditions.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.360
In such scenarios,

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:00.420
the most important signal for us to be visible is STOP.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.360
So which colour should we choose for STOP?

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.940
Here's a spectrum chart of visible light.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.580
Which colours are most visible to you here?

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.180
You'd probably say the ones in the middle, right?

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.860
The human eye is most sensitive to Green colour,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.440
followed by Yellow and Blue.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.580
So Green should be our STOP signal right?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.400
Not so fast!

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.500
We also have to take the background into consideration here.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.840
During the day, the colours exhibited by our surroundings

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.900
are mostly Green, Yellow, and Blue.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.520
So, Green would not contrast well with the background.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.300
Red is the colour that contrasts best with these colours.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.480
Also, there is another factor that comes into play here.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.980
When light travels a certain distance

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.900
it gets scattered and we see a blurred image.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.700
Out of all the colours,

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.740
Red scatters the least and Violet the most.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.880
So Red becomes a suitable choice for the STOP signal.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:12.360
Now what about the other two signal lights?

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.480
These are required when we are close enough to the traffic signal.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.020
And hence, the above mentioned factors don't matter much.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.600
So we can use any two of Green,

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.300
Yellow or Blue for the GO and CAUTION signal.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.120
Historically, along with the Red

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.200
these two colours were selected

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.780
and implemented by the railroads in the earlier 20th century.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.100
And afterwards,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.040
the same scheme was transferred for traffic signals.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.240
You might also be surprised to find out

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.340
that the middle colour isn't Yellow, but it's Amber

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.280
which is a mix of Yellow and Orange.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.800
So this kind of explains the probable reason

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.300
for choosing these colours.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.520
But is it always these three colours?

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.520
Did you know that there are countries

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.560
which have chosen Blue over Green as their GO signal?

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.320
Why don't you try and find the names of these countries,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.400
and tell us in the comments section.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.640
Hold on!

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.480
We based our answer on how visible different colours are to us.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.980
But, why is one colour more visible to us than the other?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.040
What do you think?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.940
Well, it depends majorly on our eyes.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.660
Why?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:33.160
The components of our eyes are similar to that of a camera.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.280
We know that depending on its hardware and software,

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.480
the image we see differs from camera to camera.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.400
Similarly, how we see things in real life

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.260
differs from person to person.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.000
For instance, one person may see a sight like this,

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.280
while a Red and Green colourblind person

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.600
will perceive the same sight like this.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.840
So the different components present in our eyes,

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.400
determine the way we see things.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.380
To know more about the Components of eyes

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.940
visit the link in the description below!

